@* Re-renders its content whenever the engine's hosts, selection or store change.

   Pages wrap their body in this rather than each subscribing to two events and remembering to
   unsubscribe. The store raises a change per affected row, so this is the one place that decides
   how a store change becomes a render.

   One rule comes with it: **anything that reads the store must be inside this component.** A
   re-render here re-invokes the child content, and nothing else. A value computed above the tag is
   captured by the child-content closure when the *page* renders, so it is never recomputed — the
   containers list once showed "Running" indefinitely for a container stopped from a terminal for
   exactly this reason. `PageChromeScope` counts: a toolbar subtitle built from the store goes
   inside too. *@
@implements IDisposable
@inject EngineManager Engine

@ChildContent

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        Engine.Changed += OnChanged;
        Engine.Store.Changed += OnStoreChanged;
    }

    void OnChanged() => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    void OnStoreChanged(StoreChange _) => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    public void Dispose()
    {
        Engine.Changed -= OnChanged;
        Engine.Store.Changed -= OnStoreChanged;
    }
}
